# Supabase: ask before acting

Never run commands against the live Supabase project, database, or MCP without explicit permission in this conversation.

## Requires permission first

Ask and wait for a yes before doing any of the following:

- Supabase MCP tools that hit the project (SQL, tables, migrations, logs, advisors, edge functions, branches, keys, pause/restore, cost, etc.)
- Supabase CLI against a linked or remote project (`supabase db`, `supabase migration`, `supabase functions`, `supabase gen`, and similar)
- Executing SQL, applying migrations, changing schema, RLS, storage, auth, or Edge Functions
- Creating, pausing, restoring, or otherwise mutating a Supabase project

Describe what you want to run and why, then wait. Do not treat prior chats, docs, or "I'll just check" as approval.

## Allowed without asking

- Reading local code, env examples, and docs
- Planning SQL/migrations and showing them for review
- Editing local files only (client code, local migration files) when the user already asked for that work
- Fetching public Supabase documentation

If the user says no, stop. Do not retry the same live operation with a different tool.
